DejaVu Modifications (Public Domain)
====================================

The DejaVu modifications are in the public domain, as are the contents of
the DejaVu fonts subdirectory (the directories containing the DejaVu
fonts). The DejaVu modifications are also available under the Bitstream
Vera and Arev licenses described above, at your choice.

The DejaVu fonts are a superset of the Bitstream Vera fonts, with the
addition of the Cyrillic, Greek, Armenian, Hebrew, Arabic, Thai, Georgian,
Devanagari, Ethiopic, Cherokee, and IPA character sets, as well as many
other miscellaneous glyphs from a number of other scripts.

The sources for these modifications are available on the DejaVu
project page (see https://dejavu-fonts.github.io/).

The DejaVu fonts are distributed under the same terms as the original
Bitstream Vera fonts and Arev fonts; this license file is included to
document the license terms as they apply to the DejaVu fonts.

Upstream URL: https://dejavu-fonts.github.io/
